We know, $\cos ^2 \alpha+\cos ^2 \beta+\cos ^2 \gamma=1\Rightarrow \cos ^2 \alpha+\cos ^2 \beta=1-\cos ^2 \gamma=\sin ^2 \gamma\therefore$ Statement 1 is correct.
Now, $\cos ^2 \alpha+\cos ^2 \beta+\cos ^2 \gamma=1\begin{aligned}
& \Rightarrow 1-\sin ^2 \alpha+1-\sin ^2 \beta+1-\sin ^2 \gamma=1 \\& \Rightarrow 3-\left(\sin ^2 \alpha+\sin ^2 \beta+\sin ^2 \gamma\right)=1 \\& \Rightarrow \sin ^2 \alpha+\sin ^2 \beta+\sin ^2 \gamma=2\end{aligned}\therefore$ Statement 3 is correct.
